{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be","id":74925,"title":"Is Werewolf: The Forsaken the game you want it to be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-19T06:16:15-08:00","id":74925,"title":"Is Werewolf: The Forsaken the game you want it to be?","content":"I've been thinking about this for a little while now, and I think the focus on the spirit world over connections to both humans and wolves may make the werewolf title entirely misleading. For the most part when one approaches a werewolf story they expect it to be from the perspective of humans hunting down a beasts that eats them, this is no different from what used to be the standard approach to vampire stories.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness is different in that it makes the monster the protagonist, but I've been thinking lately the perhaps a big part of Werewolf\u2019s problem is that it's too different from expectations. Now spirits have come up frequently as a subject in other werewolf fiction, but it's never to the committed extent werewolf adheres too. In fact, werewolf throws out a lot of the drama of the lycanthropic situation from a horror perspective. Replacing it with a mythic heritage that involves a strange Eden, an active overzealous father and an insane mother (unfortunate implications ahoy!), alternative creation myths aren\u2019t really given any attention, this is just considered to be \u2018the truth\u2019, because\u2026 werewolf oral traditions are so reliable? The spirits (your enemies) told you so? What? It falls a little flat with too much thinking, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are one of the most removed from human creatures the World of Darkness creators have come up with, with the only justification for human involvement seeming to be for the purpose of reproduction. I don't know if I'm alone in this but that seems uncomfortable and like it can go in a lot of dark, but not necessarily fun directions. And when you think about it, why are Werewolves the most inhuman of the world of darkness creatures? They\u2019re at least half human, yet their morality holds them farther apart than any of the other supernaturals. Now, certainly spirits can be compelling and interesting antagonists and reference points, but it seems like a lot has been lost because of them.<br /> <br /> Gifts and Renown, the werewolf magic tied intimately to spirits has to be one of the least interesting point of the game, and isn't anywhere near as compelling as other supernatural powers. Rites, being more versatile and less tied directly to spirits fair slightly better. Lunacy is another mechanic attributed to spirits (well, one spirit) that seems to mostly get in the way of telling interesting stories, reducing the threat of humans finding out about werewolves to what amount to a DM Fiat with how difficult it is to overcome.<br /> <br /> Werewolves pack structure is represented in most werewolf stories, but it's also based entirely off of modern myths, when the reality might actually be more interesting. I mean, if werewolves behaved like actual wolves and their pack was literally their blood relations, each werewolf has a substantially weaker family that they're responsible for, a family that likely is human(more or less) that has human issues with their monster relative who\u2019s just trying to do the best for them (even when they\u2019re not right about what that is). And honestly, I don't think I'm the only one that thinks that werewolf-human interaction might make for a more interesting story than bargaining with spirits that are arbitrarily unreasonable.<br /> <br /> Of the main three gamelines, despite being usually the second in release, Werewolf has had the least material printed for it before going to PDF format.<br /> <br /> This isn't meant to drum up hate towards the game, I\u2019m looking forward to the new edition, but\u2026 has anyone asked these questions to the developers? Because this is the sort of reaction I get from my players when I bring up running a werewolf game.<br /> <br /> So what do you think? Is Werewolf the game you want it to be? And if not, what should werewolf be about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:10:18-08:00","id":74944,"title":"","content":"Concerns like this have been brought up in the what do you want to see in the idigam chronicle thread. I made a similar comment there. Ultimately though, I think the animistic spirit side of werewolf is a central part of the game's identity. Fans of werewolf as it stands currently would likely not be interested in the update if it did away with the spirit aspect, and I wouldn't blame them -it would not be the same game without it. I do think, however, that an effort should be made to play up the human/wolf dichotomy to a similar extent that the flesh/spirit dichotomy currently is. I think which aspect gets more focus should be left up to the ST, so chronicles focused on either are equally easy to run. And I believe that concern has been heard and is being taken into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:26:05-08:00","id":74950,"title":"","content":"For me, YES, It is <i><b>exactly </b></i>what I wanted it to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It is my favorite of the Lines, with Changeling coming next. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:50:05-08:00","id":74959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=74950#post74950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, YES, It is <i><b>exactly </b></i>what I wanted it to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It is my favorite of the Lines, with Changeling coming next. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mine too. I think the big problem is the same the other main three had, with their corebooks not being very informative and, in some cases, being overly cautious about 'power.' It is very easy to read the core book and not realize that the Pure look any different from the Forsaken (which led to our first game being a sort of paranoid gangwar, where you didn't know if your neighbors were Pure or not until they came for you).<br /> <br /> That said, if the changes in Blood and Smoke are anything to go by, they do seem to recognize what happened with these corebooks and are willing to fix and improve them. Power from the start is a good rule to go by.<br /> <br /> I don't believe changing the fluff to make the game unrecognizable would be a good idea, and I'm pretty sure the developer, having been involved with the game lines of both Werewolves, is aware of what people like and dislike, particularly since there's been threads about it across three different forums they've participated in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:53:01-08:00","id":74963,"title":"","content":"What Charlaquin said. I would add only that I\u2019d like to see the rules tweaked in such a way that those of us who want to emphasize the human/woof dichotomy and to downplay or ignore the spirit/flesh dichotomy will be able to do so without needing to houserule half the game. In particular, give wereolves toys to play with that aren\u2019t hardwired to interacting with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T09:33:48-08:00","id":75008,"title":"","content":"Do not forget about the human perspective. There should be a disconnect and contrast between all things human and all things werewolf, and this should scare the PCs, especially if they're these newly changed werewolves with all their pre-change baggage, trying to adapt to being a predator in the vast, uncaring Darwinist nightmare that is the setting.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do crazy scary things, sometimes because they can't stop themselves from doing so, sometimes because they choose to do so. They kill strangers who lack the requisite pure blood for the sin of loving and desiring their wolfblooded kin. They follow arcane laws of the Shadow that are hard to understand but which breaking, even if you don't know you've done it, gets the wolves and spirits bearing down on you. They <i>eat people</i>, because nothing is as fulfilling and spiritually potent and addictive to them as human meat.<br /> <br /> This should terrify the protagonists. They should be thinking &quot;is this what I am going to become?&quot; How will they balance the needs of everyday human existence - friends, family, hobbies, a job, money, children - with the demands of being a hunter and a killer? This duality is what makes the game interesting.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, being the least human mindsetted supernaturals in the game, have the most human ties. While Vampires and Mages often sever or alienate their prevous life, family, and such, werewolves latch on and hold onto it with rabid fervor. It's these little things they can't just leave, and abandon to go fight some war of attrition on the other side of the world. And to know that htose hateful things will try and hurt them, just to hurt you, is also interesting ot me. The Azlu that eats your sister's brain to utterly mess with you. The spirit that Urged your brother to commit suicide. The Ivory Talon who manipulated the bank to forclose your childhood home. These are things you just don't see. The war is much more personal, more lowkey, and to me, more interesting, as its something I can see myself trying to fight for as a person, rather then the Apocalypse &quot;Why do we even try?&quot; feel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:01:13-08:00","id":75071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75008#post75008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not forget about the human perspective. There should be a disconnect and contrast between all things human and all things werewolf, and this should scare the PCs, especially if they're these newly changed werewolves with all their pre-change baggage, trying to adapt to being a predator in the vast, uncaring Darwinist nightmare that is the setting.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do crazy scary things, sometimes because they can't stop themselves from doing so, sometimes because they choose to do so. They kill strangers who lack the requisite pure blood for the sin of loving and desiring their wolfblooded kin. They follow arcane laws of the Shadow that are hard to understand but which breaking, even if you don't know you've done it, gets the wolves and spirits bearing down on you. They <i>eat people</i>, because nothing is as fulfilling and spiritually potent and addictive to them as human meat.<br /> <br /> This should terrify the protagonists. They should be thinking &quot;is this what I am going to become?&quot; How will they balance the needs of everyday human existence - friends, family, hobbies, a job, money, children - with the demands of being a hunter and a killer? This duality is what makes the game interesting.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, being the least human mindsetted supernaturals in the game, have the most human ties. While Vampires and Mages often sever or alienate their prevous life, family, and such, werewolves latch on and hold onto it with rabid fervor. It's these little things they can't just leave, and abandon to go fight some war of attrition on the other side of the world. And to know that htose hateful things will try and hurt them, just to hurt you, is also interesting ot me. The Azlu that eats your sister's brain to utterly mess with you. The spirit that Urged your brother to commit suicide. The Ivory Talon who manipulated the bank to forclose your childhood home. These are things you just don't see. The war is much more personal, more lowkey, and to me, more interesting, as its something I can see myself trying to fight for as a person, rather then the Apocalypse &quot;Why do we even try?&quot; feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my experience this is entirely inaccurate. Both in play and from the source material, a Werewolves alien mindset is rarely mentioned as a cause for drama. It seems like the attitude of the text has been universally &quot;Werewolf abruptly completely change their morality rules at the first change, and then don't change back. Because.&quot; (From a design standpoint, it seems to have no purpose other than to cause Werewolves to strictly interact with each other and spirits and completely disregard humans, while other supernaturals who's calling isn't specifically... death, don't tend to.) Honestly, I think you're supposing that werewolf is a better game than it actually is. You don't really get anywhere by not looking over something's flaws.<br /> <br /> I can't say much for the Apocalypse. I haven't had too much experience with the game, everything I've read seems to indicate it has all the problems of the Forsaken thematically, but inflated due to age and questionable moral rambling by the designers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:23:41-08:00","id":75086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75071#post75071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my experience this is entirely inaccurate. Both in play and from the source material, a Werewolves alien mindset is rarely mentioned as a cause for drama. It seems like the attitude of the text has been universally &quot;Werewolf abruptly completely change their morality rules at the first change, and then don't change back. Because.&quot; (From a design standpoint, it seems to have no purpose other than to cause Werewolves to strictly interact with each other and spirits and completely disregard humans, while other supernaturals who's calling isn't specifically... death, don't tend to.) Honestly, I think you're supposing that werewolf is a better game than it actually is. You don't really get anywhere by not looking over something's flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that it is entirely possible - and I can't speak for anyone else here - that others may just disagree with you and find things in the game that you haven't yet, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:26:18-08:00","id":75087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75071#post75071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the attitude of the text has been universally &quot;Werewolf abruptly completely change their morality rules at the first change, and then don't change back. Because.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that &quot;a non-negligibly-frequent problem in werewolf society concerns werewolves having trouble cutting ties with their human lives&quot; is a thing it's not hard to pick up on from the text and the shift to Harmony is as &quot;abrupt&quot; as any other replacement of Morality/Integrity, I find it difficult to trust your reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:33:38-08:00","id":75092,"title":"","content":"The books tend to figure you're starting your game a fair amount of time after your First Change. Enough that you've been tutored and taught about the various tribes and vows, and that's why you have gifts and rituals, because you learned them during that time. This saves the storyteller from having to have sessions where an NPC tells them everything in the core rulebook so the players understand what the tribes are, what the auspices are, that they can change into five forms and so forth. It doesn't mean that the First Change occurs and you instantly switch settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:35:20-08:00","id":75094,"title":"","content":"For me, as I think I said in the thread about &quot;what we want to see in the Idigam chronicle&quot;, no, it was not.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, Apocalypse was not quite what I wanted either, even though I think it appealed to me more all things said.<br /> <br /> I think there is a rather big problem:<br /> <br /> Werewolves do not have the same easily adaptable sources as vampires or mages or even changelings do.<br /> <br /> We got the story of the vampire's side with &quot;Interview with the Vampire&quot; and similar books, that worked rather well.<br /> <br /> Werewolves though have a lot of horror stories that are either about them being the monster to be hunted, OR of them not really being in control at all, being a victim and a monster.<br /> That does not really work for an rpg line (you can run it, but it will likely be a bit short and not easy to built a long story out of), while Vampire could adapt that formula of narrating the eternal unlife of its stars.<br /> <br /> Classical legends of werewolves often ave a strong link with curses, or magic, devil pacts (werewolf trials in the middle ages) and such, some of that might have served as a good basis, but this, I think is what we got with Skin Changers in a rather acceptable form.<br /> <br /> Both Apocalypse and Forsaken did a lot of inventing for the very basic concepts, I think that is why they have the problem of not being necessarily what a werewolf fan wants.<br /> <br /> <br /> For my part, if I have to cite a good werewolf story which I think is a nice basis for an roleplaying game, it would most likely be the anime Wolf's Rain.<br /> It was technically the very opposite of werewolves (wolves who assumed a human &quot;glamour&quot; instead of actually changing shape), but it did the sense of living among humans but not being one quite well, the struggle, the drama, the issue of forming a pack out of wildly different personalities...<br /> It also explored the connection between humans and wolves quite well and was, amusingly also about a kind of coming Apocalypse and the role wolves played in it.<br /> <br /> I do think that the aspect of animism is not a bad choice, shapeshifter legends tend to go well with that shamanistic vibe, not only in the Americas. Spirits, the way they are presented, can really encompass a great amount of supernatural beings over the whole world, you can do a lot with them and I think if Forsaken has a problem about spirits, then it is perhaps that it has too much generalizations.<br /> Their relationship with the Urathra, their hierarchies, their behaviour...<br /> <br /> I also think the Art of Forsaken was not really my thing.<br /> It did try to be freaky, full of body horror and similar a bit too much for my taste...<br /> I would have preferred a bit more of a &quot;natural terror&quot;, more of the scaryness of tooth and claw and the dark instead...<br /> Most of the other lines had art that spoke to me, werewolf did too, but I guess it was rather evident just from the visuals that we would not really get along well...<br /> <br /> The game has its mood, it is not quite the one I had been hoping for...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:08:33-08:00","id":75151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/75136-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-new-oskana-chronicle-overhaul-post-gmc\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/75136-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-new-oskana-chronicle-overhaul-post-gmc\"> Werewolf the Forsaken: The New Oskana Chronicle Overhaul (post GMC) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/75136-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-new-oskana-chronicle-overhaul-post-gmc\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/75136-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-new-oskana-chronicle-overhaul-post-gmc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Werewolf: the Forsaken New Oskana Overhaul Document (http://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing) While this is what we're using for our own chronicle, primarily it's a full blown W:tF overhaul. It could use input and commentary as much of it needs ongoing </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's specifically the directions I want Werewolf: the Forsaken to take; the difference is that myself and another author have already begun to overhaul it some time back. Best way I can sum it up. So in answer to the basic question? No. Werewolf the Forsaken is -not- the game I want it be, despite being one of my favorites and once being my favorite of the Nwod line (that changed as time went on, especially post GMC). I won't reiterate much more here; I've spoken at essay length on the Idigam Chronicle thread and elsewhere, so the easiest way is just to look over there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:20:20-08:00","id":75166,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I think Knit's problem is he's never, ever seen how a low (starting at 5) Harmony werewolf is quite horrifying, from the shapeshifter standpoint. Take, let's say, an Iron Master at Harmony 4, which would start rolling Kuruth if he can't check his smartphone every 10 minutes (while awake). The Hunter in Darkness who needs to compulsively hunt, kill and eat it's prey, who lives in a dense neighborhood, and - who has already depleted the population of stray cats and dogs too thin... what's he gonna hunt now? People.<br /> <br /> And these? these are born from a spiritual malady - the ban-like behaviours that the Uratha are subjected to.<br /> <br /> But to answer your question? yes, it's exactly the game I want.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:21:02-08:00","id":75168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75087#post75087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that &quot;a non-negligibly-frequent problem in werewolf society concerns werewolves having trouble cutting ties with their human lives&quot; is a thing it's not hard to pick up on from the text and the shift to Harmony is as &quot;abrupt&quot; as any other replacement of Morality/Integrity, I find it difficult to trust your reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one line does little to address the actual amount of relevance and focus it has (or more accurately the lack thereof) it has throughout the entire damn gameline. Sorry, I can cherry pick brief references to my heart's content, but it won't change a distinct lack of material (in the corebook specifically) to address a -major fucking facet- of werewolf existence that gets brushed under the rug in the very book it should have a hard look at. It doesn't. If it's so frequent, you'd expect a -bit- more focus on it from the onset. The fact of the matter? It doesn't. His problem isn't the reading. His problem is the lack of material to actually back that up as something noteworthy within the essential core aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> It's like having a few brief references to that scattered throughout suppliments, or maybe a chapter much later in the gameline's development for Vampire that addresses something like... I dunno... masquerading as a human and the difficulties it causes, or the troubles involved with the transition into undeath. It deserved quite a bit more than it got, which is basically an afterthought.<br /> <br /> Big difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 02-19-2014, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:32:32-08:00","id":75174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75168#post75168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It deserved quite a bit more than it got, which is basically an afterthought.<br /> <br /> Big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>My constant fucking refrain in the what-do-you-want-to-see thread has been &quot;consolidate all the important information that's scattered throughout the supplements&quot; and I take issue with people taking lack of clarity as an excuse to outright make things up to complain about. The corebook is not great. That much is virtually unanimous. The corebook is not <i>the entire </i><i>gameline</i>, which means I have no qualms with telling people they're mistaken when they confuse the former and the latter.<br /> <br /> It's not cherry-picking when you can shake an entire bushel off of any branch except the dead one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:56:15-08:00","id":75190,"title":"","content":"In an attempt to be fair.<br /> I obviously agree that more succinct information should be in the corebook, as does pretty much everyone else. We'd love extra books (it's been forever since Forsaken got a good one), but the core needs to form the core of information for those books.<br /> However. nWoD was made as a toolkit. The reason for no, 'this is what happens with your social contacts when you undergo the first change' is probably because it depends entirely on the individual character. For every Uratha that cuts their ties entirely, there's another that's grown up around wolfblooded and Uratha, and another that actually spends less time with their new kind and tries to live their normal lives, except for special occasions. For every Uratha who had friends they can never keep in contact with again, there's another who now has the power to rise to the top of their organization and be the boss of bosses. There's corporate sharks, weapons dealers, doctors who pump themselves full of drugs thinking the whole thing is a psychotic break they have to stave off, kids who get kidnapped and brainwashed by folks their parents hired to fix their behavioral problems, upstanding members of society and family men and women and party boys and girls and police officers and convicts and soldiers and terrorists, and that's just from the NPCs in the books, add your own imagination and there's a billion other things that could happen.<br /> So putting down a definitive, 'This is what happens,' would only serve to keep you from doing things.<br /> And all THAT said, Blood of the Wolf goes into the more common psychological and physiological changes upon becoming Uratha. <br /> <br /> So since we've already established what is or isn't in the books, why not give an idea of what you want that aspect of the game to be like? Do you think werewolves should lose all their friends and be loners who can only stand to be around other Uratha? Or the opposite? Or some middle ground?<br /> <br /> But we're really not sticking to the thread topic anymore, which was effectively, 'Do you like Werewolf the Forsaken?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:13:05-08:00","id":75203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75168#post75168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That one line does little to address the actual amount of relevance and focus it has (or more accurately the lack thereof) it has throughout the entire damn gameline. Sorry, I can cherry pick brief references to my heart's content, but it won't change a distinct lack of material (in the corebook specifically) to address a -major fucking facet- of werewolf existence that gets brushed under the rug in the very book it should have a hard look at. It doesn't. If it's so frequent, you'd expect a -bit- more focus on it from the onset. The fact of the matter? It doesn't. His problem isn't the reading. His problem is the lack of material to actually back that up as something noteworthy within the essential core aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> It's like having a few brief references to that scattered throughout suppliments, or maybe a chapter much later in the gameline's development for Vampire that addresses something like... I dunno... masquerading as a human and the difficulties it causes, or the troubles involved with the transition into undeath. It deserved quite a bit more than it got, which is basically an afterthought.<br /> <br /> Big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, happily, there is a book coming out wherein a portion of its purpose is to clarify things that were unclear in the original core book. Let's face it, as much as folks love the game, the core book isn't the best from a reading perspective. <br /> <br /> So, we'll see what gets put out on the blog or whatever. Again, I'm not Stew, so I don't know what's going on inside his brain meats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:23:21-08:00","id":75208,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure everyone in this thread was already aware of that, Strider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:44:59-08:00","id":75227,"title":"","content":"And yet, they somehow keep missing some of the big points that comes with that.<br /> <br /> As for me, I went into WtF wanting to get werewolves. I did-a very unique batch of werewolves. It's become more than the game I wanted it to be, and I am, for now, satisfied. I will be more satisfied once it's updated of course, but as it is I like the game.<br /> <br /> Now, is it the game I want about werewolves now, personal fondness for the series asides? Hmm...maybe not. But I think the game about werewolves that I want is perhaps more arthouse-y than White Wolf would do for a main game line, and I wouldn't want them to bend backwards. What they have is good and I like it, and I can get my werewolves elsewhere, I'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:51:38-08:00","id":75237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75208#post75208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure everyone in this thread was already aware of that, Strider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are you complaining about a book's lack of clarity when the new book is going to fix exactly that and replace the former? Do you think the developers and writing team are unaware of that? Because I can assure you that is not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:53:19-08:00","id":75242,"title":"","content":"Then why is there the thread at all? And why are people commenting in it? I made no insinuations about the developers being unaware. The question was asked. It got answers. We do not have any current access to Idigam Chronicles, even in any details changes right now, so it seems pretty reasonable to address if the game as it stands is where we want it. That was the thread's entire point; addressing the game -as it is now-.<br /> <br /> Have you read Idigam Chronicles Strider? Are you on the writer's team? <br /> <br /> Until we have that material, it's pretty useless to the discussion at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 02-19-2014, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:57:58-08:00","id":75246,"title":"","content":"I happen to love the current appearance of Forsaken (over all mind you, I own every book in some form or another). Doesn't mean I don't welcome a rule set. I think people are just too used to linearity of the apocalypse line and are expecting something like that. With Forsaken, I feel it pushing my creativity. The fact that you can completely ignore some history and use others also helps. Again, it's all rumors. The only facts are the things associated with the oath, and that's due in part to the fact that it makes you friggin crazy after a time. A harmony 1 or zi'ir werewolf is a pretty scary concept to become, and all the while you may or may not know it's happening to you. <br /> <br /> Horror film werewolves may well be low harmony bale hounds of violence... or any other werewolf for that matter with a taste of the herd. <br /> <br /> A fun typical storyline might be a wolf blooded about to turn, stalked relentlessly by a tribe trying to do damage control in a freshly 'manicured' part of their territory. The wolf blooded thinks they're being haunted by creatures of the night up until the turn, when you can go very &quot;american werewolf in x&quot; with it. <br /> <br /> As for good werewolf books... try Hemlock Grove. Excellent book. Might also try the howling... Donna Boyd's collection of romance/scifi devoncroix trilogy is nicely tragic (although not exactly proper for this setting). hm... Wolf's Rain isn't perfect by a large margin... Skin Walkers as a movie was a good local Forsaken vs Pure style conflict. Ginger Snaps could make for a good first change reference... What's some other werewolf books I've read... It'll come to me after I close this thread I know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:06:14-08:00","id":75251,"title":"","content":"I deeply love Forsaken and have had a great deal of fun with the Chronicles of it that I've run but, as per the <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?666785-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-What-s-missing-and-what-could-change-in-a-Revised-edition\" target=\"_blank\">massive thread on RPG.net</a> I started... er, early last year I think? Well, as anyone who read that can see, I think there's plenty of mileage to improve it.<br /> <br /> So I guess I'm fortunate that I'm on the writing team <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, thread was from nearly 2 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:15:44-08:00","id":75261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75251#post75251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I deeply love Forsaken and have had a great deal of fun with the Chronicles of it that I've run but, as per the <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?666785-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-What-s-missing-and-what-could-change-in-a-Revised-edition\" target=\"_blank\">massive thread on RPG.net</a> I started... er, early last year I think? Well, as anyone who read that can see, I think there's plenty of mileage to improve it.<br /> <br /> So I guess I'm fortunate that I'm on the writing team <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, thread was from nearly 2 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you entirely, Chris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T19:42:53-08:00","id":75392,"title":"","content":"Books similar to Requiem's clanbooks? Yes, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T20:00:22-08:00","id":75399,"title":"","content":"Oooo that'd be something. I also wouldn't mind custom swag for the series either. Forsaken damage counters or some such... essence points? I've got the forsaken dice from years ago, used in tandem with the vampire dice (i use the red ones for st creatures pools so as not to confuse my players)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T03:13:41-08:00","id":75507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75399#post75399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooo that'd be something. I also wouldn't mind custom swag for the series either. Forsaken damage counters or some such... essence points? I've got the forsaken dice from years ago, used in tandem with the vampire dice (i use the red ones for st creatures pools so as not to confuse my players)</div> </div> </div> </div>Custom swag would be pretty cool, but I seem to remember that with the Mummy: the Curse Kickstarter there was an issue with doing cool extras like dice these days - I honestly can't remember what the particular problem was, though.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't be surprised if a Wolf Must Hunt Conditions Cards set was done, like the one for Blood &amp; Smoke, although I must emphasise that this is just speculation on my part rather than having inside knowledge.<br /> <br /> I would fight everybody ever at once if it meant I could get in on doing the Werewolf equivalent of Requiem Clanbooks. I think they'd probably have to be Tribebooks rather than Auspicebooks, but man, I'd love that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T04:06:44-08:00","id":75520,"title":"","content":"Edit: Disregard, question was answered in a different thread.<br /> <br /> As for was Forsaken the game I wanted it to be? All in all, yes.<br /> <br /> There's very little material for werewolves as protagonists, and while it can be done in, say, Pathfinder, I like the unique touch White Wolf gave them. I've tweaked the hell out of them for my own purposes, but I did the same to vampires and mages as well.<br /> <br /> I don't know what all is going to be in The Idigam Chronicle but given how excellent a job the team did on Blood and Smoke, I have every confidence it'll be a rreshing new breath on a much-enjoyed game line. Sorry for typo, forum won't let me backspace for some reason and I'm too lazy to delete, copy, and paste from a word doc.<br /> <br /> Forsaken is the game I wanted it to be because it gave me an idea, a template, that I could take and use as I wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","user":"Nickpire84","date":". 02-20-2014, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T04:22:44-08:00","id":75524,"title":"","content":"My unpopular opinion is that &quot;Werewolf&quot; conjures up a bunch of preconceptions, and then you get a game that feels much more like &quot;Shaman&quot; than anything else. I know the spirit stuff is core to the game, but it's never been terribly compelling, and certainly isn't the first thing that springs to mind. Fury. Loss of control. The clash of humanity and animal instinct. Waking up with blood in your mouth and on your hands. Being terrified at what you've become, how you can't reasonably fit in with society well. That sort of stuff. The game as-is is difficult to pitch to people, and I wish there was a bit more horror to it. It doesn't help that The Pure are pretty lame antagonists (they feel like early Sabbat more than anything, and not in a good way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-20-2014, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T05:59:01-08:00","id":75556,"title":"","content":"On that I do feel inclined to disagree. I love the Pure as antagonists. So much more nuanced than the Black Spiral Dancers of Apocalypse, and with a particularly fun and interesting sourcebook to their name. My players dread the mention of the Pure, but in a good &quot;oh shit&quot; way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T06:30:00-08:00","id":75568,"title":"","content":"Outside of the lazy sidebar reinforcements of how bad and hateful etc (show, don't tell? They do more of the latter in that &quot;but they're really nasty! Oooh oooh... be careful!&quot; way). they are in The Pure, honestly their Tribal concepts make a whole lot of sense. The insular purity driven Ivory Claws, the feral human-hating Predator Kings, the Cult of Spirit (well in part) Fire Touched. I can readily see how they'd come about as a werewolf phenomenon in the game's context without even worrying about the Firstborn mythos. They seem like natural, extremist facets of how a werewolf culture might react when things go bad. Given they're half human and how lines get so readily and violently drawn there from philosophical and other outlooks, I like their inclusion, including as PCs.<br /> <br /> If they had a treatment, it should be on par with the Covenants in Blood and Smoke; otherwise they're just anecdotes without enough core content to make them very viable (the old Forsaken Core really didn't spend much time on them there either even as pure antagonists, no pun intended). If they're presented, there should be the basic tools to have them playable, otherwise they may as well be akin to Fallen Clan/Covenant listings, or a condensed section like the Jiang Shih reference to get -some- basic utility from them. Personally, I'd prefer a Covenant level treatment; if they're a major problem and a direct, common (if not most populous in North America) werewolf faction, they really should have a nice chunk of space put towards them. An overfocus on external threats via Idigam, Shartha, Spirits etc with a lack of it on them could pose problems all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:37:13-08:00","id":75602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75507#post75507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Custom swag would be pretty cool, but I seem to remember that with the Mummy: the Curse Kickstarter there was an issue with doing cool extras like dice these days - I honestly can't remember what the particular problem was, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has something to do with the expense of &quot;printing&quot; them on-demand, but that's a half-remembered thing, so don't quote me on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't be surprised if a Wolf Must Hunt Conditions Cards set was done, like the one for Blood &amp; Smoke, although I must emphasise that this is just speculation on my part rather than having inside knowledge. </div> </div> </div>That would be pretty awesome, and would fit a trend. There are Condition Cards for GMC and B&amp;S (and Demon is getting them too if I recall properly), so it would make sense for Forsaken to get them too. No insider knowledge here either, just speculation/following the trend on my part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would fight everybody ever at once if it meant I could get in on doing the Werewolf equivalent of Requiem Clanbooks. I think they'd probably have to be Tribebooks rather than Auspicebooks, but man, I'd love that. </div> </div> </div>I already told Stew I'd volunteer for all the things post-Idigam Chronicles, but yeah, those would be awesome to work on. Also, a dedicated Bale Hounds book instead of a chapter in another book would be cool. (Nothing against <b>Blasphemies </b>- it's a great book, I just think the Hounds deserve a bigger book is all.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:54:11-08:00","id":75619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75242#post75242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why is there the thread at all? And why are people commenting in it? I made no insinuations about the developers being unaware. The question was asked. It got answers. We do not have any current access to Idigam Chronicles, even in any details changes right now, so it seems pretty reasonable to address if the game as it stands is where we want it. That was the thread's entire point; addressing the game -as it is now-.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's fine, and addressing the game as it is now is (of course) all any of us can do. And that includes the writing team. Stew's the boss man, so what information gets posted is squarely in his wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you read Idigam Chronicles Strider? Are you on the writer's team? </div> </div> </div>I haven't read it yet because we haven't written it yet. It's in progress. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And also, yes. I wasn't ignoring you earlier, and my apologies if it may have came across that way. I wanted to double-check with Stew to make sure I could say things yet. I always assume a &quot;no&quot; on that front until the developer tells me otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until we have that material, it's pretty useless to the discussion at hand. </div> </div> </div>And that's fair. I just couldn't wrap my head around complaining about the core book being less-than-ideal for people in terms of readability and so on (which is, at least in my impression, a wide spread opinion around here) when the upcoming book is expressly designed to make those clarifications. From having read the writer's bible and outline for the book, I can assure you that we are aware of the issues folks have with the current core book, and we're taking steps to address that.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the content of those two manuscripts, of course, but.....wow. Just, wow. Let's just say I am very excited to be on the team, and I'm looking forward to where <b>Werewolf </b>goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:55:14-08:00","id":75620,"title":"","content":"See, that makes a WHOLE lot more sense there Strider. Lacking context, it didn't, so apologies on my end. Without realizing you had access to some of the materials people like myself, well, don't. We're pretty clueless, so it's pretty useless for us to make assumptions we don't have a whiff of. Honestly, this hush-hush level going on has been a real bugger to contend with.<br /> <br /> I still have (how many more months, maybe more) before Idigiam chronicles comes out to run a game with W:tF present. I'm very critical (like folks couldn't tell) about a lot of areas in RPGs; mostly because I'd rather go out and change/fix/alter things than sit and wait and play damage control rather than addressing something directly. Head-on approaches unfortunately can turn fairly confrontational, but, what can I say, I'm not very complacent at all on this sorta thing. When we need to &quot;just wait and see&quot; without the vaguest glimmer on what's being brought up to bat, it's hard to present a positive face in light of what we -do- have currently that could use changing/updating. Generally, if it ain't broke, you don't fix it, unless a better option comes around. A lot of the friction going on is specifically because folks don't see eye to eye on what constitutes &quot;okay&quot;, &quot;broken&quot; and &quot;better options for it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping somewhat soon we get some hints as to what we can look forwards to, I know it'd mean less headache for my own and my co-st's own overhaul work, and if we should brace for adopting Idigam chronicles (in whole or in part), or just continue doing our own thing, or what..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":".  Clarity. 02-20-2014, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T08:38:13-08:00","id":75649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=75620#post75620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that makes a WHOLE lot more sense there Strider. Lacking context, it didn't, so apologies on my end. Without realizing you had access to some of the materials people like myself, well, don't. We're pretty clueless, so it's pretty useless for us to make assumptions we don't have a whiff of. Honestly, this hush-hush level going on has been a real bugger to contend with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable, and I wasn't trying to be confrontational myself. Nor was I intending to be coy about my involvement - like I said, I assume I can't talk about my involvement on a project until/unless I'm told otherwise. I find that best when NDA's are involved. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, again, dissemination of information is Stew's gig, so that's above my pay grade. I'll talk about what I can when I can, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still have (how many more months, maybe more) before Idigiam chronicles comes out to run a game with W:tF present. I'm very critical (like folks couldn't tell) about a lot of areas in RPGs; mostly because I'd rather go out and change/fix/alter things than sit and wait and play damage control rather than addressing something directly. Head-on approaches unfortunately can turn fairly confrontational, but, what can I say, I'm not very complacent at all on this sorta thing. When we need to &quot;just wait and see&quot; without the vaguest glimmer on what's being brought up to bat, it's hard to present a positive face in light of what we -do- have currently that could use changing/updating. Generally, if it ain't broke, you don't fix it, unless a better option comes around. A lot of the friction going on is specifically because folks don't see eye to eye on what constitutes &quot;okay&quot;, &quot;broken&quot; and &quot;better options for it&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I think that, personally, I have far fewer problems with Werewolf as written than you do. That doesn't mean that I don't want to see any changes, though. Of course what works for me might not work for you, and vice-versa. I hope people enjoy what we're doing, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm hoping somewhat soon we get some hints as to what we can look forwards to, I know it'd mean less headache for my own and my co-st's own overhaul work, and if we should brace for adopting Idigam chronicles (in whole or in part), or just continue doing our own thing, or what.. </div> </div> </div>We'll see. I have no idea when Stew is going to post blog stuff, sorry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:34:01-08:00","id":75683,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty positive there will be approaches in Idigam Chronicles that will make me personally go &quot;That, THAT, more of that&quot; as a given; it's been a rare nWoD book lately that didn't. Then again, I'm not one for light paint strokes either; &quot;But don't change it TOO much&quot; is what crippled many of the earlier nWoD books, so my perspective is to go hog wild and see how far something can be taken. Blood and Smoke is like that; there's very little mechanically unchanged, shuffled around or re-addressed. Basic concepts are certainly still intact, but it's anything but a light brush stroke that was taken to it. The result? Many players who did not like or had no interest in Requiem praising it and being invested in the game.<br /> <br /> If I have any real concerns right now for Idigam Chronicles, is that the brush strokes applied won't be heavy enough to draw in the people that otherwise were dissatisfied, -especially- with the often maligned statement of &quot;It doesn't feel Werewolf enough&quot;. It's a common thing, and in part due to the presentation of werewolves having little to do with humans, which flies right in the face of popular culture notions; the very ones that draw people to the games to begin with. For people who don't want much changed... we have the old Forsaken already. We've got basic rules updates all over the forums. Hell, the folks that loved the W:tA nods (I didn't personally), the conversion book and W:tA 20th ed to cull from.<br /> <br /> That's where I start to go &quot;well shit...&quot;. Sometimes games work as presented for folks, sometimes they don't, it's unavoidable; but I'm very concerned that the changes we're getting are going to be too heavily predicated on concerns of alienating the old fan-base diehards instead of standing on it's own as just a damn good product, changes be damned. Call it a misplaced concern, as it may well be (and I acknowldge that); but after looking at some of the bulk of the more active posters (outside of myself, because I'm one stubborn fuck at times), the areas I've seen consistently presented as primary concern (too weak Gauru, cleaned up gifts, an intact renown system) would -not- in of themselves draw new players in to give the game another chance given my own experiences. Basically running Forsaken through a GMC stopgap... nothing would really change for the better in regards to drawing new players in, though it may satisfy some portions (and I emphasize, portions) of the existing fan base.<br /> <br /> So lets sum it up this way: I'm really hoping it doesn't turn into a one step forward, another step back situation where the devs and writers hold back running wild in some areas with new edition because &quot;it might alienate existing fans&quot;. If it's a quality, awesome product, it'll stand on its own, changes regardless. And to be blunt, the game could use more new fans. I don't see catering to people satisfied mostly with what is present as beneficial with a new edition if it holds back that running wild and testing of boundaries. Or brushing off their concerns when they're present throughout the community (I'm not saying you're doing this Strider, for clarity's sake). &quot;Oh, but that wasn't present before, or is too big a change; I like it as it is overall, lets not fiddle with it heavily&quot;. I find few things more toxic to game development, and after 17 years of dealing with LARPS and TT's and rewrites and house rules and custom made this and that's among other things that I got tired of light touch approaches. Nothing is more disappointing than buying a new edition of a game, and getting very little new content, beyond some rules tweaks that could be summed up in a small document. It honestly makes some of us feel ripped off and conned that it just wasn't handed out as an errata or similar.<br /> <br /> It's one things to keep them in mind, it's entirely another to work with them. There's a reason why there's actually something of a fairly strong divide among Forsaken fans on the game, and why consistent problems surface with new players who take a look at the game. I want that addressed far more than turning Gauru form into a damn tank, because that's honestly trivial by comparison. Make sense? My tone is likely entirely off here, or perhaps my meaning, but I'm not sure how better to articulate it. Keeping in mind of course, outside of being a stubborn fuck, I can be a cynical bastard too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T10:05:57-08:00","id":75713,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for any of the other writers (as I'm not them), although I strongly suspect they agree with me when I say I want this to be the most kick-ass Werewolf book yet. I am a huge Werewolf fan. I spent quite a few years in the Camarilla (now Mind's Eye Society) acting as a Storyteller and cheerleader for the game, holding Regional and Global Storytelling positions multiple times (and sometimes simultaneously) almost constantly from 2005 - 2011. I put in tons of effort to get the word out about the game, talk to people about what they didn't like (and did like, of course!), try to get folks to play the game, and so on.<br /> <br /> I don't say that as a way to pat myself on the back or anything. It's just there so that when I say this is truly a labor of love for me, you know I mean it. For the parts I'm writing, I simply won't allow anything other than my personal best writing ever. It's simply not in me to do so.<br /> <br /> Will everyone like every part of the book? No, not at all. In fact, that would be a silly expectation, I should think. But the goal is to make the best damn Werewolf book we can, and I have every iota of faith that we will do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T16:31:37-08:00","id":75947,"title":"","content":"I'm jonesin for some new rules. And that Anthology book, hardcore. Been reading through the strix anthology and I'm loving it. I bought blood and smoke pdf on a whim, now im lookin at actually running a game of that.<br /> <br /> Course I'm also looking to the new W20 stuff as well, particularly the White Howler Tribebook, but I'm itching for Idigam a whole lot more.<br /> <br /> Strider, Ya'll just keep doin what you're doin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T16:56:20-08:00","id":75957,"title":"","content":"Roger roger. *salutes*<br /> <br /> There is some seriously scary stuff that's going to be in the book. (Scary in a good way, don't worry.) I'm incredibly excited to work on this.<br /> <br /> (Also, yinz guys can just call me Jim. It's cool. I mean, it's my name and in my signature 'n stuff.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:03:29-08:00","id":76115,"title":"","content":"Looking back at the initial release of Forsaken, I absolutely agree the fiction anthology is needed and wanted. If nothing more than to have a frame of reference to inform my visualization of the game. I want the players and ST to all be on the same page when it comes to how they picture the setting. I'd like the fiction help play up there's more to a werewolf's world than what they see, the other senses being just as important as sight is to a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T02:11:35-08:00","id":76148,"title":"","content":"I'd be very, very game for a fiction anthology myself; using a Classic WoD game as an example, the only reason I got into, and gave D:tF a chance was the novels for it. They were evocative, gave the game a lot of context and a means to look at what the game would look like in actual practice from a narrative stand point. I ended up loving D:tF as a result from that additional perspective.<br /> <br /> I fully agree with Darksider here; if possible an Anthology style collection of stories could go a long way to fleshing things out and making it easier to grasp. Sometimes a deeper exploration of the game's themes via that medium (rather than shorter chapter blurbs for the supplements, which I prefer short in the RPG books themselves) go a long, long way. I think it'd go a long way to help smoothing some of the rougher spots by seeing it in a narrative flow (the transition from Integrity to Harmony, things like that). <br /> <br /> Since I'm a critical bastard though, and taking the Strix Anthology (which I have and read through) as an example; it'd likely be best if it didn't exist in a game setting vacuum. The former was heavily predicated on being an existing fan of the game for the majority of the stories and knowing a lot of the ins and outs and nuances; as a new reader, a lot of this was lost on folks who didn't have that level of familiarity. If the anthology was more, I'm not sure the word I'm looking for is basic, but at least dealing with some more core-things, it could go a long way to drawing new players in along with ramping up additional interest in Idigam Chronicles. I'm a bit biased here, but I'd love to see a werewolf story or two by Greg Stolze (I've loved everything I've read by him regarding WW and Unknown Armies). <br /> <br /> I realize that such game novels aren't always popular (and to be blunt, it often has more to do with the quality of the writing than them being game setting novels; look at the popularity of the 40K and Shadowrun novels for a good example of how they can sell like hot cakes when consistent in quality), or even profitable, but... if there was room for it, I think quite a few people would gain a much clearer POV on W:tF with their inclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T04:20:02-08:00","id":76181,"title":"","content":"For me, while I loved the fluff of the game I just could never get passed the, imo, terrible mechanics. I've tried to play it multiple times and I just can't get into it. I'm hoping the new chronicles book will fix it, because as I said, I really do love the themes and fluff present in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T05:37:11-08:00","id":76215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76181#post76181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, while I loved the fluff of the game I just could never get passed the, imo, terrible mechanics. I've tried to play it multiple times and I just can't get into it. I'm hoping the new chronicles book will fix it, because as I said, I really do love the themes and fluff present in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular areas of mechanics that you found problematic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:19:05-08:00","id":76225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76215#post76215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any particular areas of mechanics that you found problematic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Just about everything. The gifts, imo, weren't worth their cost, and their dicepools were all over the place. The &quot;war form&quot; wasn't that great for combat, and was easily overshadowed by lesser forms using guns or some sort of fighting style. While beneficial, I felt that the willpower requirements for resisting Lunacy were much too high, leading to encounters with mundane people feeling fairly trivial. I recall Renown being something I didn't care much for, I think due to some sort of restrictions it places on something or another, though I can't quite recall the exact issue I had with it. Throw in an issue or two I have with spirits in general and you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:47:56-08:00","id":76244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76225#post76225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Just about everything. The gifts, imo, weren't worth their cost, and their dicepools were all over the place. The &quot;war form&quot; wasn't that great for combat, and was easily overshadowed by lesser forms using guns or some sort of fighting style. While beneficial, I felt that the willpower requirements for resisting Lunacy were much too high, leading to encounters with mundane people feeling fairly trivial. I recall Renown being something I didn't care much for, I think due to some sort of restrictions it places on something or another, though I can't quite recall the exact issue I had with it. Throw in an issue or two I have with spirits in general and you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Renown part, was the issue more of what Renown does, or it existing in the first place?<br /> <br /> And what issue did you have with spirits? Was it mechanical (in which case I'd suggest taking a look at the God-Machine Chronicle rules, which you can get for free <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-The-God-Machine-Rules-Update?term=God-Machine\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.) Or was it how the spirit/Uratha dynamic worked? Or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:29:48-08:00","id":76445,"title":"","content":"When I first picked up <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, I thought the experience was going to me much like the one I had with <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. I expected a lot of what was in <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> to be brought over, but stripped down to archetypes and not stereotypes, and focused on the individual player-character level struggles, not the world-spanning problems. I had very little interest in <b>Apocalypse</b>, but since I've almost spent more time as an ST than as a player, I made sure to always have the corebooks from all the lines in case I was asked to run one of them or introduce elements from that game. So, I bought <b>Forsaken</b> expecting it to collect dust more often than be read.<br /> <br /> What I got was many of the conventions of <b>Apocalypse </b>flipped on its head and instead of fuzzy superheroes, what I was given was Uratha, The People. People with a duty to their family, their tribe (or Tribes) and to their race as a whole. I got a family with one big promise expected of the children - keep up the family tradition. I got a proper respect of the heritage of shape-shifting (it comes from animism, folks, it's that damn old!) and all the old traditions that come with it. I got The People, who understand that the separations between flesh and spirit or animal and man are false and they <i>know it</i> because they can <i>see it</i>. Every day, all around them, right there in front of their eyes. I got the children of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, the Great Hunter and the Queen of Air and Darkness. Gods of the Shadow Realm giving birth to tiny, fleeting lives because <i>they </i>wanted to be part of the cycle of life. Those children being the products of passion and gaining the gifts (and Gifts) of such a heritage. The power of the Wolf, the flexibility of the Moon, the drive to Hunt, and all while being something that's fully human or animal or flesh or spirit, but a balancing force between all those things. Gone were the spirits to continually praised their &quot;oh so worthy protectors&quot; who tried to claim that everything that came after them was &quot;unclean&quot;. Instead I got a Spirit Realm that placed werewolves firmly within the food chain, no better or worse than any other predators, as long as they could hold their own. Also gone were the wolf-men running around in full war form developing elaborate martial arts and complex rituals. The beast-man was now for one thing - kill everything in sight - and like all such weapons, it was dangerous and not something to be toyed with. There were no more Rage traits, just rage. There were no more Great Caerns, just &quot;our territory&quot;. There were no more epic warriors, just The People. People who struggle every day with what they see around them and use what advantages they have to make their little corner of the world better.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the question, yes,<b> Werewolf: the Forsaken </b>is the game I want it to be, but that I never <i>expected </i>it to be.<br /> <br /> But that's just my opinion, I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:25:18-08:00","id":76486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76445#post76445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first picked up <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, I thought the experience was going to me much like the one I had with <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. I expected a lot of what was in <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> to be brought over, but stripped down to archetypes and not stereotypes, and focused on the individual player-character level struggles, not the world-spanning problems. I had very little interest in <b>Apocalypse</b>, but since I've almost spent more time as an ST than as a player, I made sure to always have the corebooks from all the lines in case I was asked to run one of them or introduce elements from that game. So, I bought <b>Forsaken</b> expecting it to collect dust more often than be read.<br /> <br /> What I got was many of the conventions of <b>Apocalypse </b>flipped on its head and instead of fuzzy superheroes, what I was given was Uratha, The People. People with a duty to their family, their tribe (or Tribes) and to their race as a whole. I got a family with one big promise expected of the children - keep up the family tradition. I got a proper respect of the heritage of shape-shifting (it comes from animism, folks, it's that damn old!) and all the old traditions that come with it. I got The People, who understand that the separations between flesh and spirit or animal and man are false and they <i>know it</i> because they can <i>see it</i>. Every day, all around them, right there in front of their eyes. I got the children of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, the Great Hunter and the Queen of Air and Darkness. Gods of the Shadow Realm giving birth to tiny, fleeting lives because <i>they </i>wanted to be part of the cycle of life. Those children being the products of passion and gaining the gifts (and Gifts) of such a heritage. The power of the Wolf, the flexibility of the Moon, the drive to Hunt, and all while being something that's fully human or animal or flesh or spirit, but a balancing force between all those things. Gone were the spirits to continually praised their &quot;oh so worthy protectors&quot; who tried to claim that everything that came after them was &quot;unclean&quot;. Instead I got a Spirit Realm that placed werewolves firmly within the food chain, no better or worse than any other predators, as long as they could hold their own. Also gone were the wolf-men running around in full war form developing elaborate martial arts and complex rituals. The beast-man was now for one thing - kill everything in sight - and like all such weapons, it was dangerous and not something to be toyed with. There were no more Rage traits, just rage. There were no more Great Caerns, just &quot;our territory&quot;. There were no more epic warriors, just The People. People who struggle every day with what they see around them and use what advantages they have to make their little corner of the world better.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the question, yes,<b> Werewolf: the Forsaken </b>is the game I want it to be, but that I never <i>expected </i>it to be.<br /> <br /> But that's just my opinion, I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. So much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:43:45-08:00","id":76501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76445#post76445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first picked up <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, I thought the experience was going to me much like the one I had with <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. I expected a lot of what was in <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> to be brought over, but stripped down to archetypes and not stereotypes, and focused on the individual player-character level struggles, not the world-spanning problems. I had very little interest in <b>Apocalypse</b>, but since I've almost spent more time as an ST than as a player, I made sure to always have the corebooks from all the lines in case I was asked to run one of them or introduce elements from that game. So, I bought <b>Forsaken</b> expecting it to collect dust more often than be read.<br /> <br /> What I got was many of the conventions of <b>Apocalypse </b>flipped on its head and instead of fuzzy superheroes, what I was given was Uratha, The People. People with a duty to their family, their tribe (or Tribes) and to their race as a whole. I got a family with one big promise expected of the children - keep up the family tradition. I got a proper respect of the heritage of shape-shifting (it comes from animism, folks, it's that damn old!) and all the old traditions that come with it. I got The People, who understand that the separations between flesh and spirit or animal and man are false and they <i>know it</i> because they can <i>see it</i>. Every day, all around them, right there in front of their eyes. I got the children of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, the Great Hunter and the Queen of Air and Darkness. Gods of the Shadow Realm giving birth to tiny, fleeting lives because <i>they </i>wanted to be part of the cycle of life. Those children being the products of passion and gaining the gifts (and Gifts) of such a heritage. The power of the Wolf, the flexibility of the Moon, the drive to Hunt, and all while being something that's fully human or animal or flesh or spirit, but a balancing force between all those things. Gone were the spirits to continually praised their &quot;oh so worthy protectors&quot; who tried to claim that everything that came after them was &quot;unclean&quot;. Instead I got a Spirit Realm that placed werewolves firmly within the food chain, no better or worse than any other predators, as long as they could hold their own. Also gone were the wolf-men running around in full war form developing elaborate martial arts and complex rituals. The beast-man was now for one thing - kill everything in sight - and like all such weapons, it was dangerous and not something to be toyed with. There were no more Rage traits, just rage. There were no more Great Caerns, just &quot;our territory&quot;. There were no more epic warriors, just The People. People who struggle every day with what they see around them and use what advantages they have to make their little corner of the world better.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the question, yes,<b> Werewolf: the Forsaken </b>is the game I want it to be, but that I never <i>expected </i>it to be.<br /> <br /> But that's just my opinion, I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said, and I hope that <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> continues in this vein for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:49:24-08:00","id":76660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76244#post76244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Renown part, was the issue more of what Renown does, or it existing in the first place?<br /> <br /> And what issue did you have with spirits? Was it mechanical (in which case I'd suggest taking a look at the God-Machine Chronicle rules, which you can get for free <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-The-God-Machine-Rules-Update?term=God-Machine\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.) Or was it how the spirit/Uratha dynamic worked? Or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just mechanics. While I like the idea of renown, I recall it just kinda turning into a huge xp dump that wasn't even close to being worth what was put into it. I'd have to go look up what all renown does to get more specific, but that was the general idea.<br /> <br /> For spirits, my biggest beef has always been their base stats. It is just so easy for spirits to have really bloated stats, making their attacks, and usually more importantly their defenses, really hard to deal with since you have to try to get through a mountain of numbers to do anything. Yes, a mountain spirit should be tough, and sure, a wind spirit should be hard to hit, but damn.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, a lot of things may or may not have been fixed by the GMC, or any future books that come out, I'm primarily just talking the old core books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:12:52-08:00","id":76748,"title":"","content":"One of the big things with Renown was it capped the max dot-level of gifts you could get. And no renown, I believe, could be higher than your primary one. Might be wrong in that one.<br /> <br /> When you got renown, you'd get a free gift from that auspice or tribe or something, which was nice. And we all know Renown is meant to be 'you perform an act of valor or wisdom, now you can get a renown,' but the way it's purchased seems like, 'Okay now I have to buy a Wisdom Renown.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-21-2014, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:57:12-08:00","id":76773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76660#post76660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just mechanics. While I like the idea of renown, I recall it just kinda turning into a huge xp dump that wasn't even close to being worth what was put into it. I'd have to go look up what all renown does to get more specific, but that was the general idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, thanks for answering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For spirits, my biggest beef has always been their base stats. It is just so easy for spirits to have really bloated stats, making their attacks, and usually more importantly their defenses, really hard to deal with since you have to try to get through a mountain of numbers to do anything. Yes, a mountain spirit should be tough, and sure, a wind spirit should be hard to hit, but damn.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, a lot of things may or may not have been fixed by the GMC, or any future books that come out, I'm primarily just talking the old core books. </div> </div> </div>Well, the spirit rules did change in GMC; notably, spirits use the lower of their Power or Finesse for their Defense now, instead of the higher (except for Rank 1 spirits). Also, spirits all have a Bane in addition to a Ban, so someone who figures out a spirit's Bane can inflict Aggravated damage to it. And so on and so forth; I'm not going to go through all of the mechanics here, when it's all available in the free GMC rules update.<br /> <br /> So hopefully all of your concerns are addressed adequately for you between the two books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:24:11-08:00","id":76801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76773#post76773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, thanks for answering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, the spirit rules did change in GMC; notably, spirits use the lower of their Power or Finesse for their Defense now, instead of the higher (except for Rank 1 spirits). Also, spirits all have a Bane in addition to a Ban, so someone who figures out a spirit's Bane can inflict Aggravated damage to it. And so on and so forth; I'm not going to go through all of the mechanics here, when it's all available in the free GMC rules update.<br /> <br /> So hopefully all of your concerns are addressed adequately for you between the two books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that sounds like it fixes most of my complaints about spirit rules, which was a relevant factor in why I didn't play more werewolf. And from what I've heard on the subject of the new chronicles book for werewolves I'm fairly hopeful that all of my other issues will be, at the very least, considerably lessened. Can't wait! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T21:53:06-08:00","id":76866,"title":"","content":"Wait a second - what did you hear? Do we have a leak? Because we have a Brute Squad* that can fix that right quick.<br /> <br /> <br /> * - If we do, I don't know about it yet, so assume I'm making this up. That's probably for the best for everyone. *sagenods*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T22:10:20-08:00","id":76872,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure at some point I heard mention of werewolves being able to better deal with spirits inherently, though that very well may have just been a suggestion that I'm remembering as something else. That said, the things I've heard about from the other gamelines chronicle books gives me a lot of hope that werewolf will be given similar treatments, which in itself would fix most of my issues with werewolf mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T00:36:40-08:00","id":76901,"title":"","content":"That's not a leak from idigam, that's a &quot;leak&quot; from God machine Chronicle (can it be a leak if the book's been out for a year?) which includes a rule about werewolves that makes them better able to cope with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T04:52:55-08:00","id":76980,"title":"","content":"That's close enough, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T05:54:39-08:00","id":77012,"title":"","content":"Yeah Dave beat me to answering that one. That is, in fact, in the <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> book, and so is not a leak. Forget what I said before about Brute Squads. In fact, I don't even know what you're talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:21:44-08:00","id":77080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=77012#post77012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah Dave beat me to answering that one. That is, in fact, in the <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> book, and so is not a leak. Forget what I said before about Brute Squads. In fact, I don't even know what you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, guess I could be a bit clearer. What I'm saying is that the mechanical and thematical updates from both Blood and Smoke as well as the teases and nudges dropped by Dave about the FWC all seem to be really well done, interesting, and high quality work. If the coming chronicles book for werewolf is as good as B&amp;S, or how the FWC is being hinted to be, I'm optimistic that it will fix most of the problems I have with the gameline it pertains to as the others have/are-being-hinted-towards-doing for theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:57:42-08:00","id":77099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=76501#post76501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well said, and I hope that <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> continues in this vein for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it'll be of the quality I've come to expect. I've seen few sour notes in this NWOD. But I'm still not done reading the main GMC book, so we'll see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T09:55:02-08:00","id":77144,"title":"","content":"If GMC has a flat note, I've yet to find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:44:46-08:00","id":77329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=77099#post77099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it'll be of the quality I've come to expect. I've seen few sour notes in this NWOD. But I'm still not done reading the main GMC book, so we'll see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought GMC was pretty amazing, and B&amp;S is great, so....we've got a trend to continue. That's all I'll say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:13:27-08:00","id":78265,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, the bane rules make things much more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T01:07:42-08:00","id":79183,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget that the bane rules and the honorary rank rules, taken together, allow werewolves to tear apart low-ranking spirits with just their claws and teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T02:46:29-08:00","id":79211,"title":"","content":"Or y'know. Hugging them for a while. (I'd make their bane a werewolf's claws and fangs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T06:07:55-08:00","id":79285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=79211#post79211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or y'know. Hugging them for a while. (I'd make their bane a werewolf's claws and fangs)</div> </div> </div> </div>True story: I've had to do that in a game, because the ST made that the Ban for a nightmare spirit. (It was something like that, anyway.) My Storm Lord was incredibly embarrassed, but did it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T06:16:26-08:00","id":79288,"title":"","content":"Some relevant excerpts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">The hierarchical nature of ephemeral beings also plays a part \u2014 Rank isn't a social convention for them but a funda-mental part of their nature. Ephemeral entities of 2 Ranks or more higher than an opponent of the same type (a Rank 5 spirit attacking a Rank 3 spirit, for example) count as their opponent's bane when using unarmed attacks, claws, or teeth.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> page 222</div>and<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">Some supernatural creatures that are closely related to a form of ephemeral being have \u201chonorary\u201d Rank in the appropriate otherworldly hierarchy; Sin-Eaters are all Bound to a ghost, for example, and werewolves are treated with respect by spirits according to their Renown.<br /> <br /> Technicalities count, in this case, but only against the ephemeral entity. A werewolf who \u201coutranks\u201d a minor spirit will deal devastating wounds to it with his claws, but a high-Rank spirit can't burn that werewolf by touching him. There are other ways to assert dominance; high-Rank entities are quite capable of showing the half-fleshed who's boss.</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u201cHonorary Rank\u201d, <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> page 221</div>Because werewolves with at least 8 total Renown start with an Honorary Rank of 3, they automatically count as a Bane to Rank 1 spirits, in addition to whatever the spirit\u2019s <i>actual</i> Bane is. When they reach Honorary Rank 4 (16 Renown), they automatically count as a Bane to Rank 2 spirits. Werewolves with Honorary Rank 5 (24 Renown) count as banes for Rank 3 spirits. Per the new Ephemeral Beings rules, werewolves interact with sufficiently low-ranking spirits as if they were solid; and such spirits are harmed just by being touched by the werewolf. This <i>alone</i> goes a long way to helping werewolves deal with spirits; and it incentivizes werewolves to invest in Renown.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d like to see <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> accelerate the relationship between total Renown and Honorary Rank to something like, say, a base Honorary Rank of 2, plus one for every <i>five</i> full dots of Renown. That would let endgame werewolves get up to Honorary Rank 7, just shy of Mother Luna, and would allow such werewolves to tear through even Rank 5 spirits without any special preparations.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Honorary Rank should vary by the type of Renown (e.g., 2 + Honor or 2 + Wisdom), and every spirit should resonate with one type of Renown: so when confronting a Glory spirit that\u2019s Rank 3, an Uratha with Glory \u2022\u2022\u2022 or more would be able to tear into it. Short form: if your Renown that resonates with the spirit in question equals or exceeds its Rank, you count as a Bane for it. Since every werewolf has a few points of Renown to start, there would always be some kind of spirit that\u2019s vulnerable to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-25-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T06:36:03-08:00","id":79294,"title":"","content":"According to <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, p.272, a werewolf with 0-7 Renown is Honorary Spirit Rank 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T10:18:32-08:00","id":79423,"title":"","content":"Although you need to note, of course, that said chart won't necessarily be the same as the means for calculating honourary rank in Idigam Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Please note, this is not a teaser, hint or other piece of new information about what the honourary rank system in IC <i>will</i> be - just me pointing out that stuff is changing, and there's every chance that the old system for rank calc might be one of the things that gets amended - especially given the way the new rule for interaction between honourary rank and spirits works.<br /> <br /> My <i>personal</i> opinion is that the old W:tF table for calculating your honourary rank is both a bit blah and overly complex at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T10:49:57-08:00","id":79445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=79423#post79423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although you need to note, of course, that said chart won't necessarily be the same as the means for calculating honourary rank in Idigam Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Please note, this is not a teaser, hint or other piece of new information about what the honourary rank system in IC <i>will</i> be - just me pointing out that stuff is changing, and there's every chance that the old system for rank calc might be one of the things that gets amended - especially given the way the new rule for interaction between honourary rank and spirits works.<br /> <br /> My <i>personal</i> opinion is that the old W:tF table for calculating your honourary rank is both a bit blah and overly complex at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is why I only cited the currently printed book is all. I hope I didn't confuse anyone - if so, my apologies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:26:34-08:00","id":79495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=79423#post79423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although you need to note, of course, that said chart won't necessarily be the same as the means for calculating honourary rank in Idigam Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure strider1276 first posted that before I posted my first edit to the post just before it; I had originally said that I thought that every werewolf starts with at least Honorary Rank 3. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=79423#post79423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please note, this is not a teaser, hint or other piece of new information about what the honourary rank system in IC <i>will</i> be - just me pointing out that stuff is changing, and there's every chance that the old system for rank calc might be one of the things that gets amended - especially given the way the new rule for interaction between honourary rank and spirits works.<br /> <br /> My <i>personal</i> opinion is that the old W:tF table for calculating your honourary rank is both a bit blah and overly complex at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>One trend I\u2019ve noticed in GMC has been a streamlining of the math. I don\u2019t know what <b>IC</b> is going to do, obviously; but replacing \u201c2 + (sum of Renowns) \u00f7 8, drop fractions\u201d with \u201c2 + relevant Renown\u201d strikes me as the sort of change that it would go with: it\u2019s much simpler, increases the significance of Renown considerably, and plays up the differences between the types of Renown, all at once. <br /> <br /> Heck, you might even have a sixth type of Honorary Rank based on Primal Urge, a catch-all that\u2019s used for interacting with the minority of spirits that don\u2019t resonate with any of the Renowns. Since Primal Urge is a one-to-ten trait, you\u2019d have to say something like every even level of it gives you an additional dot of Honorary Rank when dealing with unaligned spirits (or maybe just Sols and Lunes; WtF has a history of not aligning things relating to Father Wolf or Mother Luna with Renown), or that the increases start kicking in with Primal Urge 6, depending on how harsh you\u2019re aiming to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:57:58-08:00","id":79615,"title":"","content":"Or add PU dots to the renown count. That would make Red Sticks Rank 5, for instance. Maybe Rank 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T14:31:13-08:00","id":79640,"title":"","content":"I guess. But I\u2019d personally rather get away from the current formula for Honorary Rank altogether: like Acrozatarim, it strikes me as both a bit blah and overly complex at the same time. The only things I\u2019d salvage from it are the notion that werewolves start at Honorary Rank 2 and that Renown increases it from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:27:06-08:00","id":79691,"title":"","content":"&quot;Is forsaken the game I want it to be?&quot; is an interesting question to me. I didnt play apocolypse and media/stories of being a werewolf are few and far between. That said I had no expectations of what a game would be from a werewolves perspective beyond &quot;you're a werewolf.&quot; When I began reading the core book the mythology made sense to me. An ancient paradise ruled over by gods and constantly under siege by otherworldy entities was interesting but what was more interesting was it had that theme of &quot;nothing lasts forever&quot;.<br /> <br /> As more books have been released Ive collected most of them and been decently happy. Forsaken has some great writing, good ideas, and plenty of room for the Storyteller to adapt the world to their universe. I can see why some people dont like the original mythology surrounding Forsaken society but blasphemies basicly gave free reign to write new creation myths. I found that thoughtful and interesting. Yes more attention is payed toward Father wolf and pangea but I think thats more likely because its the creation myth thats believed the most. I look at it like living in Iran and expecting Christian or Hindu philosophies to get the same treatment as Islamic philosophies. It seems unreasonable<br /> <br /> Territories was IMO the most needed book. The territory is supposed to be a living, breathing thing and that book made it so. Territory became a character in itself that the forsaken desperately wanted to take care of similar to the Spirit binding most packs together.<br /> <br /> Lore of the forsaken and Predators expanded on spirits, spirit life, courts, and the shadow itself.<br /> <br /> Blood of the wolf expanded on what it was to be a werewolf and wolfblooded.<br /> <br /> The Rage (which contains the only representation of the blood talons I like), tribes of the moon, and Blood of the wolf all expanded on tribal and auspice affiliation.<br /> <br /> Everything that I think needed expansion and more explanation has been taken care of and theres even been more expansion on things that I would have never thought of (Things that should not have been for example). This brings me back to the original question. &quot;Is forsaken the game I want it to be?&quot;. Yes, for the most part. Coming to the core book with the simplest expectations really helped me to get into the story that is the werewolf venue. The various books have addressed my questions and even encouraged a huge amount of creative freedom which IMO shows a very mature line thats ready to give the reigns to the people playing it while simultaneously giving enough narrative to tell its own story.<br /> <br /> Now is there room to improve? Sure. I would like to see more info on the bale hounds. I would like to see alternative and yet more horrific ways to earn gifts besides sucking up to or forcing spirits to teach them. I would like to see more lodges. I would like to see rules for making werewolf safe houses (similar to mages Sanctum and Sigil book). Are those things needed? Probably not, it would just be nice to have those additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2378-char","name":"Char","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T22:59:08-08:00","id":80021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=79640#post79640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess. But I\u2019d personally rather get away from the current formula for Honorary Rank altogether: like Acrozatarim, it strikes me as both a bit blah and overly complex at the same time. The only things I\u2019d salvage from it are the notion that werewolves start at Honorary Rank 2 and that Renown increases it from there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why GMC doesn't say <i>how</i> Uratha rank is calculated. I didn't want to force the Werewolf team's hand. Present-day me, working on the Idigam Chronicle, certainly appreciates 2012-me's foresight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:53:03-08:00","id":80311,"title":"","content":"This is replying to the first post in the thread, but as I understand it, going too much into the lycanthropic horror perspective might've been a bit redundant with Vampire. Although I really waffle on werewolf spirit business (I like fighting human antagonists) I understand entirely why they explored that to try to make their werewolves distinctive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T12:33:05-08:00","id":80431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=80311#post80311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is replying to the first post in the thread, but as I understand it, going too much into the lycanthropic horror perspective might've been a bit redundant with Vampire. Although I really waffle on werewolf spirit business (I like fighting human antagonists) I understand entirely why they explored that to try to make their werewolves distinctive.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can see the issue, I actually think Death Rage and Frenzy are thematically distinct enough (especially after B&amp;S) that both can explore different kinds of horror, so I do not think overlap is a major issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:41:07-08:00","id":80518,"title":"","content":"Frenzy- you flip out because something natural is making you flip out.<br /> <br /> Death rage- I GOT A FRIGGIN F ON MY TERM PAPER!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:50:43-08:00","id":80616,"title":"","content":"I think you need pretty low Harmony to flip because of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:54:49-08:00","id":80619,"title":"","content":"Well mechanics wise yeah, but reading through the core book is how it makes it appear. Like your whole life is a hair trigger waiting to &quot;DID THAT BASTARD CUT ME OFF!?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how they handle it with Idigam. Love the idea of an updated harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T18:34:00-08:00","id":80689,"title":"","content":"Really, you kinda need Harmony around 4 for that to be a Death Rage trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T20:24:02-08:00","id":80750,"title":"","content":"Things to pay attention to. If I recall correctly (I may well not), isn't frenzy check easier to fail at the lower ranks as well? It strikes me as Forsaken and Apocalypse had almost opposite mechanics with how their rage systems worked. You roll to go into frenzy (not trying to of course) and you roll to resist death rage. You start with higher harmony and more control in forsaken, where as in apocalypse you start at rank 1 (or 0) and are slightly more hair trigger. Assuming you have enough rage. I don't quite recall the rules for people with rage lower then 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:44:34-08:00","id":80840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/74925-is-werewolf-the-forsaken-the-game-you-want-it-to-be?p=80750#post80750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things to pay attention to. If I recall correctly (I may well not), isn't frenzy check easier to fail at the lower ranks as well? It strikes me as Forsaken and Apocalypse had almost opposite mechanics with how their rage systems worked. You roll to go into frenzy (not trying to of course) and you roll to resist death rage. You start with higher harmony and more control in forsaken, where as in apocalypse you start at rank 1 (or 0) and are slightly more hair trigger. Assuming you have enough rage. I don't quite recall the rules for people with rage lower then 4.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you mean Death Rage, no. It's always Resolve + Composure to resist, so Harmony doesn't affect how easy or hard it is to fail. However, what stimuli can trigger Death Rage rolls is determined by Harmony, and the lower your Harmony the more things can trigger it. All of this is Forsaken, of course. I've never played Apocalypse so I don't know how that works, and at any rate it's entirely possible for all of that to change with Idigam Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T01:52:19-08:00","id":80917,"title":"","content":"Forsaken and Apocalypse did approach this in different directions. In Forsaken you roll to resist and in Apocalypse you roll to lose control.<br /> <br /> That said, in terms of starting points and progression, they're not that different. In Forsaken you start with decent Harmony and can take a decent level of Resolve + Composure and stay in control. You risk Harmony loss and extra provocations, but you can increase Resolve+Composure over time to compensate for it (and buy back Harmony). In Apocalypse you start with low-ish Rage, making it unlikely to lose control. But as you progress you can put your control at more risk (buying more Rage because it is worth it), but you also gain better control (Rank bonuses to resist).<br /> <br /> What made Apocalypse more &quot;hair trigger&quot; at start for higher Rage Auspices was the double whammy of not being able to directly invest in ways to reduce the odds of resisting (just buy lots of WP to spend to automatically stop a Frenzy for that turn), and the massive change in odds based on moon-phase and Auspice. A starting Ahroun on the full moon had over a 50% chance of Frenzying on a Rage roll (~60% in Crinos), So a bad situation basically meant they were going to frenzy.<br /> <br /> And Apocalypse characters with permanent Rage less than 4 (or 5/6 for Garou of those respective Ranks) can Frenzy. You roll the higher of temp/perm Rage, and temp can exceed perm. So if you rile up a Rage 1 werewolf enough that they have 4 temporary Rage, they can Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}